data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"For each response, the implicit reward is $\\beta$ times (policy log-prob minus reference log-prob).\nTake the margin as chosen minus rejected. The per-pair loss is $-\\log\\sigma(\\text{margin})$, which\nequals $\\operatorname{softplus}(-\\text{margin})$. Use the split form $\\max(x,0)+\\log(1+e^{-|x|})$ with\n$x = -\\text{margin}$ so large margins stay finite. Average over pairs."},"hints_note":null}

